From 3acda15472387b1acdda417fdf5dee0786936dfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:43:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] main: set `cfg(proc_macro)` for a proc-macro crate

derive-deftly 1.12.0 (arti 2.7.0) src/lib.rs:49: "Unable to resolve `use`
target ::"derive_deftly_macros-1_12_0_H7f"::derive_deftly_engine".

derive-deftly-macros 1.12.0 declares every entry point as
`#[cfg_attr(proc_macro, proc_macro)]` and compiles a dummy `mod proc_macro`
under `#[cfg(not(proc_macro))]`, relying on rustc's `cfg(proc_macro)`,
which rustc sets whenever the crate type is proc-macro. mrustc never set
it: the plugin built against the dummy module, exported no macro, and the
facade crate's re-export found nothing.

The flag is set from the command-line crate type (what cargo and minicargo
pass), next to `cfg(test)`. The real `proc_macro` crate then comes from
the extern prelude (Expand_ProcMacro's implicit crate), as it does for
every proc-macro crate without an `extern crate proc_macro;`.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1
---

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index 44c09914..3a07c012 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -233,6 +233,14 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
     {
         Cfg_SetFlag("test");
     }
+    // rustc sets `cfg(proc_macro)` for a proc-macro crate (from the crate type). derive-deftly-macros 1.12.0 (arti
+    // 2.7.0) declares its entry points `#[cfg_attr(proc_macro, proc_macro)]` and has a dummy `mod proc_macro` for
+    // other builds: without the flag the plugin exported no macro, and `use derive_deftly_macros::derive_deftly_engine`
+    // in derive-deftly failed to resolve.
+    if( params.crate_type == ::AST::Crate::Type::ProcMacro )
+    {
+        Cfg_SetFlag("proc_macro");
+    }
 
     Expand_Init();
 
